// selfhost/hir/lib.mty
//
// v0.8 scaffolding for the self-hosted HIR + lowering package.
//
// The runnable HIR lives in `lower.mty` as a single consolidated module
// — the v0.8 `mty check` driver still compiles one `.mty` file at a
// time, same single-file constraint as the v0.4 lexer and v0.6 parser.
// This file documents the intended v0.9+ module layout once `mty-pkg`
// lands cross-file module resolution.
//
// ## v0.9+ module layout
//
//   selfhost/hir/
//     lib.mty           // this file — package root + public re-exports
//     nodes.mty         // HirFn / HirStruct / HirEnum / HirExpr / ...
//     ids.mty           // ItemId / FnId / ExprId / ... (newtype wrappers)
//     lower.mty         // CST -> HIR lowering driver (the runnable file)
//     items.mty         // item-level lowering (fn / struct / enum / ...)
//     exprs.mty         // expression-level lowering
//     types.mty         // type expression lowering
//     patterns.mty      // pattern lowering
//     dump.mty          // HIR -> human-readable dump (for diagnostics)
//
// ## Public surface
//
// The exported entry point is `lower_file()`, which walks the trusted
// Rust parser's CST through the host bridge and emits HIR "events"
// (one per item lowered, one per expr/stmt/type allocated). The bridge
// is conceptually the same as the v0.6 parser bridge — read access to
// the input (CST), write access to the output (HIR sink).
//
// pub fn lower_file() -> Unit
//
// The bootstrap test in crates/mty-driver/tests/selfhost_hir.rs
// installs a SelfhostHirHost that:
//   1. seeds the CST from the trusted Rust parser
//   2. responds to CST navigation queries (node_kind, child_count, ...)
//   3. captures the HIR event stream
//   4. compares the item-kind sequence against the Rust HIR pipeline

package selfhost_hir_lib
